# Source is always text. Without this, a stray control character (a literal NUL
# written instead of an escape sequence) makes git classify the file as binary:
# `git diff` prints "Binary files differ", `git blame` stops working, and a
# three-way merge resolves to one side without emitting conflict markers.
# `diff` forces git to diff these as text even when they do contain such a byte,
# so the problem surfaces as a visible patch instead of hiding behind "Binary".
*.ts   text diff
*.tsx  text diff
*.js   text diff
*.jsx  text diff
*.mjs  text diff
*.cjs  text diff
*.py   text diff
*.json text diff
*.css  text diff
*.md   text diff
*.yml  text diff
*.yaml text diff
